From: Andrei Kholodnyi <andrei.kholodnyi@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fast-DDS VxWorks: 10 s SHM healthy check timeout by default

A participant opening a peer's SHM port runs Port::healthy_check(): every
listener waiting on the port must show it is alive (wake up and bump its
status counter, every healthy_check_timeout_ms / 3) within
healthy_check_timeout_ms, default 1000 ms, or the port is judged "NOT Healthy"
and removed and re-created. Under QEMU on small hosts (8 vCPUs on 4 host CPUs,
60 Hz tick) the owner's listener thread missed that 1 s while the new
participant started: a live port was removed, its owner kept listening on the
removed segment and the pub/sub never connected (listener silent, CI test04 /
test06 on GitHub's 4-CPU runners).

Default to 10 s on VxWorks (listeners then wake every 3.3 s; a dead port is
detected after up to 10 s). Verified on QEMU pinned to 4 host CPUs: 10/10
talker/listener SHM rounds connect, no "NOT Healthy" (1 s: silent listener
within 1-7 rounds). Guarded by __VXWORKS__.
---
--- a/include/fastdds/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemTransportDescriptor.hpp
+++ b/include/fastdds/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemTransportDescriptor.hpp
@@ -51,7 +51,16 @@
 {
     static constexpr uint32_t shm_default_segment_size = 0;
     static constexpr uint32_t shm_default_port_queue_capacity = 512;
+#ifdef __VXWORKS__
+    //! VxWorks: a peer judges a port "NOT Healthy" and removes it when the port's listener
+    //! threads do not report within this time. Under QEMU on small hosts (8 vCPUs on 4 host
+    //! CPUs, 60 Hz tick) the owner's listener thread can miss 1 s while a new participant
+    //! starts, and a live port was removed: its owner kept listening on the removed segment
+    //! and never received data. 10 s (listeners wake every timeout / 3).
+    static constexpr uint32_t shm_default_healthy_check_timeout_ms = 10000;
+#else
     static constexpr uint32_t shm_default_healthy_check_timeout_ms = 1000;
+#endif // ifdef __VXWORKS__
     static constexpr uint32_t shm_implicit_segment_size = 512 * 1024;
 
     //! Destructor
